# VS Code REST Client scratchpad — install humao.rest-client and click "Send Request".
@base = http://localhost:8000

### health
GET {{base}}/health

### chat via the mock provider (no API key needed)
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Summarise the leave policy." }],
  "model": "mock-fast",
  "metadata": { "task_type": "summarise" }
}

### routing policy — 501 until GW-003
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "hello" }],
  "policy": "default"
}

### prometheus metrics
GET {{base}}/metrics

### who am I
GET {{base}}/auth/me

### what each role grants
GET {{base}}/auth/permissions

### create an API key — returned once, then only its hash exists
POST {{base}}/v1/api-keys
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "checkout-service",
  "environment": "test",
  "scopes": ["gateway.chat.write"]
}

### list keys — prefixes only, never the key
GET {{base}}/v1/api-keys

### chat as a service, using the key from the seed output
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer nx_test_replace_me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "hello from a service" }],
  "model": "mock-fast"
}
